{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere","id":983334,"title":"[2E] Are Orders really everwhere?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T08:23:51-07:00","id":983334,"title":"[2E] Are Orders really everwhere?","content":"I ask if Orders are having large sways in Sleeper institutions? I run game in Boston and our Mysterium player want the Order to secure him position on some collage or university. Thing is that three local major Mysterium cabals do not seems to be dedicated in securing position in those king of organisations - contrary to Seers that have Harvard and Free Council that have MIT. Also, does not having influence in Sleepers institution is shtick of whole Silver Ladder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-07-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:39:03-07:00","id":983342,"title":"","content":"You openly have one city that is void all three of the sects in the book.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are places and times none of the sects have influence in a place. There's only so many mages at any time. If you don't want him to have an easy in, he doesn't have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:51:16-07:00","id":983349,"title":"","content":"They're not everywhere, they're most places. The default. They're reasonably likely to have a presence in most places, which makes it easier for an ST to say &quot;the orders are a thing here&quot; or &quot;the orders aren't a thing here&quot; without player backlash. But if you don't want the orders to have any presence at all in a place, there is nothing stopping you from doing so and just having nameless order(s) exist there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:12:56-07:00","id":983356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere?p=983342#post983342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You openly have one city that is void all three of the sects in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you rephrase this thought? I cannot understand what it means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere?p=983349#post983349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you don't want the orders to have any presence at all in a place, there is nothing stopping you from doing so and just having nameless order(s) exist there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you get wrong my example setting to the question - and by this clue of topic. City I run game is Boston - (more or less) the same as in <b>Mage</b> 1E corebook and of <b>Boston Unveiled</b> setting book. This setting has all Pentacle Orders and Seers in number of about few dozen mages in all. Just in this setting, four official Mysterium cabals - Brotherhood of the Ineffable Truth, Company. Sanguine Laurel and White Putnams - they all sound as not interested in direct influence of campuses of universities. They like academics, but not like Sleepers and their education.<br /> <br /> So question is that Mysterium Mystery Cults are having their tentacles this deep so Order members could benefit from those connections even if no local mage is dedicated in cultivating those ties?<br /> <br /> In simple terms - <b>Does all Orders Mystery Cults work like Labyrinth of Guardians of Veil and Orders mages only need to do secret handshakes and Sleepers just give them all power in their cults? </b>They say secret code and academics just give them job on local university?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:18:39-07:00","id":983359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere?p=983356#post983356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you rephrase this thought? I cannot understand what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go reread Tuscon and then tell me if the the Pentacle Alliance or Seers of the Throne are everywhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:30:00-07:00","id":983366,"title":"","content":"For this topic, <b>l</b><b>et's assume that region we talk HAVE Pentacle and Seers Orders. </b>If then - will they just can sap any institution that more or less works with particular Order dogma by Orders Mystery Cults? Like can Mysterium just do 'Alakazam' and every university in town will enroll memebers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:59:20-07:00","id":983382,"title":"","content":"Not unless the Dean of Admissions is in the Mysterium, which seems unlikely. The Mysterium would be more interested in the research going on than in who's in the college. Though that likely means they'd get some say in staffing lab assistants and such. Not in Boston though, because except for MIT the Seers have dominated the colleges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:27:02-07:00","id":983396,"title":"","content":"If Mages really want to add someone to a university's staff they can, they use Fate and Mind to make it happen. Still that doesn't mean it's worth the effort or that sleepers won't question the placement afterwards if the Mage is an obvious misfit.<br /> \u200bPersonally, outside of Seer control freaks, I don't see the Pentacle being all that inclined to place Awakened members on a school's staff, sleepwalkers sure, but the Awakened have their own priorities and teaching freshman isn't normally one of them. I see the Mysterium, Ladder and Libertines being more likely to create separate groups and organizations that are associated with the university. Research groups, scholarship funds and activist groups. That way they have access and clout on campus without becoming too bound up in its affairs.<br /> \u200bIf your player really wants his character to have a job on campus and the Seers control them all, then maybe they can offer him a position. Just between friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 10-07-2016, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:58:02-07:00","id":983476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere?p=983396#post983396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see the Mysterium, Ladder and Libertines being more likely to create separate groups and organizations that are associated with the university.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may getting it wrong, but I always thought it was Ladder idea/goal to have hooks in Sleepers institutions. Like it's more probable that Silver Ladder will have ear of Dean of Admissions than Mysterium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-07-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:33:11-07:00","id":983500,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder has a habit of preferring institutions with certain demographics in mind, based on the Thearch's personal biases(good and bad.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:11:29-07:00","id":983744,"title":"","content":"All three orders, along with the Seers, would be interested in universities. The Mysterium focusing on the gathering and protection of knowledge, often from the sleepers in those very institutions, and the Silver Ladder and Free Council working to shape the future by influencing the thinking of the students. The Ladder would be the one of the three most likely to dig their hooks into the school's administration in order to direct policy, especially the hiring of teachers who teach the 'right' ideas (as opposed to the know your limits lessons of the Seers). The Free Council would, in my opinion, be more focused on individual programs that they feel embody humanity's continuing growth or explore human societies history that isn't a reflection of a Time Before.<br /> \u200bI still think that though the Mysterium might take a direct hand in the Anthropology department, aiming at limiting Sleeper damage to new discoveries, the Ladder and Free Council would take a more hands off approach to control. You don't have to be the admissions director if you control the scholarship and other financial programs that pay for students, or be the President when you are the ones he comes to for money to hire new professors. You can pick and choose which programs experience the most growth by controlling which ones get the most grants and donations.<br /> \u200bIf you want to know who really wields the most influence on campus just look around, they're the people with their names on the buildings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T02:41:27-07:00","id":983835,"title":"","content":"I would say no. I think that every caucus has sleepwalker members and contacts in places that interrest them but they are not everywhere the order would have interrests.<br /> <br /> And I think that the guardians is the only ones that have tight control of their sects, the ladder have limited controls and the other orders have sects depending on the current goals and projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:41:17-07:00","id":983970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983334-2e-are-orders-really-everwhere?p=983366#post983366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this topic, <b>l</b><b>et's assume that region we talk HAVE Pentacle and Seers Orders. </b>If then - will they just can sap any institution that more or less works with particular Order dogma by Orders Mystery Cults? Like can Mysterium just do 'Alakazam' and every university in town will enroll memebers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The principle is not &quot;Only regions that don't have them won't have them influencing places.&quot;<br /> <br /> The principle is &quot;If they can not be in a city, they can not be in your university.&quot;<br /> <br /> Long story short, yes, Mages do not automatically have control over all the universities in the world. Your guy does not automatically have an in, and will still have to work or cheat his way into a job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}